<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<%- include('../partials/head') %>

<body>
  <%- include('../partials/header') %>

  <main id="main-content">

    <section class="faq-hero" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
      <div class="container faq-hero__content">

        <p class="faq-badge">Help Center</p>

        <h1 id="faq-title">Frequently Asked Questions</h1>

        <p>
          Find answers to common questions about visiting Wildwood Park.
          Cannot find what you are looking for? Feel free to contact us.
        </p>

        <!-- <div class="faq-hours-card">

          <span class="faq-hours-card__icon" aria-hidden="true">
            <%- include('../partials/icons/clock') %>
          </span>

          <div>
            <p>Open Daily</p>
            <strong>9:00 AM - 6:00 PM</strong>
          </div>

        </div> -->

      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="faq-section" aria-labelledby="visiting-title">
      <div class="container faq-container">

        <!-- VISITING -->
        <h2 class="faq-category-title">Visiting the Park</h2>

        <div class="faq-list">

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>What are the park opening hours?</summary>
            <p>
              Wildwood Park is open every day from 9:00 AM to 6:00 PM.
              The last entry is at 5:00 PM to ensure all visitors have
              adequate time to enjoy the park before closing. We recommend
              arriving early to make the most of your visit.
            </p>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>How long should I allow for my visit?</summary>
            <p>
              We recommend allowing at least 4–5 hours to explore all four
              habitats and enjoy our experiences. If you plan to attend
              shows and keeper encounters, you may wish to spend a full day
              with us.
            </p>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>Is there parking available?</summary>
            <p>
              Yes, we have a large free car park with over 500 spaces.
              Accessible parking bays are located close to the main entrance.
              During peak times, overflow parking is available with a free
              shuttle service to the entrance.
            </p>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>Can I leave and re-enter the park?</summary>
            <p>
              Yes, you can leave and re-enter the park on the same day.
              Simply have your hand stamped at the exit and show it upon
              return. Please note that re-entry must be before 5:00 PM.
            </p>
          </details>

        </div>

        <!-- FACILITIES & SERVICES -->
        <h2 class="faq-category-title">Facilities &amp; Services</h2>

        <div class="faq-list">

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>Are there places to eat in the park?</summary>
            <p>
              Yes, we have several dining options including the Treetop Cafe in the
              Rainforest Canopy, Savannah Grill overlooking the plains, and Ocean View
              Restaurant by our aquatic habitat. We also have picnic areas if you prefer
              to bring your own food.
            </p>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>Are there lockers available?</summary>
            <p>
              Yes, lockers are available near the main entrance in various sizes.
              Small lockers are complimentary, while larger lockers are available for
              a small fee. We recommend storing any valuables before exploring the park.
            </p>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>Is there a gift shop?</summary>
            <p>
              Yes, our main gift shop is located at the park exit and features a wide
              range of wildlife-themed merchandise, books, toys, and souvenirs.
              Smaller shops are also located in each habitat area.
            </p>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>Are pushchairs and wheelchairs available for hire?</summary>
            <p>
              Yes, pushchairs and manual wheelchairs are available for hire on a
              first-come, first-served basis from the main entrance. A refundable
              deposit is required. We recommend booking in advance during peak periods.
            </p>
          </details>

        </div>

        <!-- ACCESSIBILITY -->
        <h2 class="faq-category-title">Accessibility</h2>

        <div class="faq-list">

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>Is the park accessible for wheelchair users?</summary>
            <p>
              Yes, Wildwood Park is fully accessible with paved pathways throughout
              all habitats. Some elevated walkways in the Rainforest Canopy have
              alternative ground-level viewing areas. Accessible toilets are located
              throughout the park.
            </p>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>Are assistance dogs permitted?</summary>
            <p>
              Yes, assistance dogs are welcome throughout the park. We ask that they
              remain on a lead at all times. Please note that some indoor exhibits may
              have restrictions for the safety of the animals, but alternative viewing
              options will be available.
            </p>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>Do you offer quiet hours or sensory-friendly sessions?</summary>
            <p>
              Yes, we host sensory-friendly mornings on the first Sunday of each month
              from 9:00 AM to 11:00 AM. During these times, we reduce audio announcements,
              dim lighting where possible, and provide quiet spaces throughout the park.
            </p>
          </details>

        </div>

        <!-- ANIMALS & CONSERVATION -->
        <h2 class="faq-category-title">Animals &amp; Conservation</h2>

        <div class="faq-list">

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>What animals can I see at the park?</summary>
            <p>
              Our four habitats are home to over 500 species. The Rainforest Canopy
              features tropical birds, monkeys, and sloths. Savannah Plains is home
              to lions, elephants, zebras, and giraffes. Reptile World houses
              crocodiles, snakes, and lizards, while Ocean Discovery features sea
              turtles, sharks, and colourful reef fish.
            </p>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>Can I feed the animals?</summary>
            <p>
              For the safety and health of our animals, feeding is only permitted
              during supervised keeper encounters and designated feeding experiences.
              Please do not feed the animals outside of these sessions.
            </p>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>How does the park support conservation?</summary>
            <p>
              Wildwood Park actively supports global conservation efforts. We
              participate in breeding programmes for endangered species, fund habitat
              protection projects worldwide, and dedicate a portion of all proceeds to
              wildlife conservation organisations.
            </p>
          </details>

        </div>

        <!-- POLICIES -->
        <h2 class="faq-category-title">Policies</h2>

        <div class="faq-list">

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>Can I bring my pet to the park?</summary>
            <p>
              Unfortunately, pets are not permitted in the park for the safety and
              welfare of our animals. The only exception is assistance dogs, which
              are welcome. Assistance animals must be registered at the entrance.
            </p>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>Is photography allowed?</summary>
            <p>
              Personal photography and video recording for non-commercial use is
              encouraged throughout the park. Flash photography is prohibited in
              certain exhibits to avoid distressing the animals. Tripods and
              professional equipment require prior permission.
            </p>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>What items are not allowed in the park?</summary>
            <p>
              For safety reasons, the following items are prohibited: drones,
              balloons, laser pointers, loudspeakers, and any items that could
              harm or disturb the animals. Large coolers and glass containers are
              also not permitted.
            </p>
          </details>

        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="faq-contact-cta">

      <div class="faq-contact-cta__content">

        <h2>Still have questions?</h2>

        <p>
          Our friendly team is here to help with any queries about your visit.
        </p>

        <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">
          Contact Us
        </a>

      </div>

    </section>

  </main>

  <%- include('../partials/footer') %>
</body>

</html>
